flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the limits decide whether the AI runs
  accDescr: A new issue, a new discussion in a category of answer_categories, an answer of the reporter or a comment of the reporter after a release asks for a run of the AI. When a maintainer asks, or someone runs the workflow by hand, the AI runs. For everyone else, a comment after a release needs the AI to have read fewer than release_replies comments of the reporter since the release. Then the day needs room: fewer than max_per_day new issues, first answers to discussions, follow-ups and replies after a release in the 24 hours before. A new issue or discussion also needs its author to have opened fewer than max_per_author_per_day issues and discussions in those 24 hours. Over a limit, the maintainer takes over, and the run notes which limit was reached.
  asks(["a new issue or discussion,<br>an answer or a comment<br>after a release"]) --> who{"a maintainer,<br>or by hand?"}
  who -- "yes" --> runs["the AI runs"]
  who -- "no" --> release{"`after a release:<br>room in<br>**release_replies**?`"}
  release -- "yes, or no release" --> day{"`room in<br>**max_per_day**?`"}
  release -- "no" --> waits["the maintainer takes over;<br>the run notes the limit"]
  day -- "no" --> waits
  day -- "yes" --> new{"`a new issue or<br>discussion: room in<br>**max_per_author_per_day**?`"}
  new -- "yes, or neither" --> runs
  new -- "no" --> waits
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef person fill:#0969da26,stroke:#0969da,stroke-width:2px
  class asks trigger
  class who,release,day,new question
  class runs ai
  class waits person
